-- title:
--   Real Lie algebra generated by exchange
-- statement:
--   The real Lie algebra $\mathfrak g_n$ generated by exchange is the smallest real vector space of $n$-qubit matrices that contains $iE_{ab}$ for every pair of distinct qubits $a\neq b$ and is closed under the commutator $[A,B]=AB-BA$. A Hamiltonian $H$ is **obtained from exchange** by scalar multiplication, addition and Lie commutators (composition laws 1–3, p.11) exactly when $iH\in\mathfrak g_n$; since $[iH,iK]=i\,(i[H,K])$, commutators of anti-Hermitian generators correspond to the Hamiltonian commutators $i[H,K]$ of law 3.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Scalars are real. No identity generator is adjoined. Unitary conjugation (law 4) is not part of the closure, because it adds nothing (milestone (4.6)). The bracket is Mathlib's commutator Lie structure on matrices.
-- source:
--   Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, Theory of Decoherence-Free Fault-Tolerant Universal Quantum Computation, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, §IV.B, p.11; Theorem 5, p.26

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_exchange

open QAlgorithms

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

namespace CollectiveDFS

/-- The real Lie algebra generated by the exchange interactions: the smallest real Lie subalgebra
of `n`-qubit matrices (bracket the commutator) containing `i E_ab` for all wires `a ≠ b`.
A Hamiltonian `H` is obtained from exchange by "scalar multiplication, addition and
Lie-commutators" (laws 1–3, Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, §IV.B, p.11, PDF p.11; Theorem 5, p.26) iff `i H` lies in it.

**Formalization Note** The bracket is the matrix commutator `⁅A, B⁆ = AB − BA`
(`LieRing.ofAssociativeRing`, a local instance in Mathlib). Scalars are real, as for Hamiltonians. The anti-Hermitian generators
`i E_ab` make the bracket `[iH, iK] = i (i[H, K])` the paper's `i[H, K]` of law 3. No identity
generator is adjoined. Unitary conjugation (law 4) is not part of the closure; it adds nothing
(`CollectiveDFS.conj_mem_exchangeLie`). -/
noncomputable def exchangeLie (n : ℕ) : LieSubalgebra ℝ (Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) :=
  LieSubalgebra.lieSpan ℝ (Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ)
    {M | ∃ a b : Fin n, a ≠ b ∧ M = Complex.I • exchange a b}

end CollectiveDFS


